        "original_id": "5ec4beb3-17dd-56f9-91ba-78355ebe5c91",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Owen Wister, Lucy Maud Montgomery\n- Works: Done in the Open, Anne of Green Gables\n- Roles: writer, historian, author\n- Topics: western fiction\n\nFacts:\n- Owen Wister was born on July 14, 1860, and he was an American writer, historian, and the \"father\" of western fiction.\n- Lucy Maud Montgomery was born on November 30, 1874, and she was a Canadian author who published as L.M. Montgomery.\n- Done in the Open was a verse collection by American author Owen Wister that was published in 1903.\n- Anne of Green Gables was first published in 1908, beginning Lucy Maud Montgomery's best-known series of novels.\n- Owen Wister died on July 21, 1938.\n- Lucy Maud Montgomery died on April 24, 1942.",
